    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0129" n="1197" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg1197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Conference files, lot 60 D 627, CF 375</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Secretary Eden to the Secretary of State
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d58-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-09-15">September 15, 1954</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Foster</hi>:] I received your message<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d58-f2"/> just as I was on the point of leaving Rome. I shall
                    be glad to see you in London on whatever day would suit you. The dates September
                    27 and 28 which you suggest for the preliminary nine power conference should, I
                    think, prove possible. We too had hoped that the E.D.C. would be passed. But
                    every country now agrees that as things are there is no present possibility of
                    reviving the supranational idea. We must encourage other forms of European
                    unity.</p>
                <p>[Kindest regards,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Anthony</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>The source text was given to Dulles by British Ambassador Makins during a meeting
                    at noon on Sept. 15. A memorandum of this conversation, prepared by Merchant, is
                    in Department of State file 740.5/9–1554.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d58-f2" n="2" xml:id="d58-f2-content">
                <p>This is a reference to Dulles’ letter of Sept. 14, <ref target="#pg1192">p.
                        1192</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
